                                "sense_id": "ee6cb4c5-9d96-3c65-993c-5cffa89d7a7e",
                                "text": "Evidence that the NSA was secretly building a vast database of U.S. telephone records - the who, the how, the when, and the where of millions of mobile calls - was the first and arguably the most explosive of the Snowden revelations published by the Guardian newspaper in 2013."
